  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return grid\n    R = len(grid)\n    C = len(grid[0])\n    nines = [(r, c) for r in range(R) for c in range(C) if grid[r][c] == 9]\n    if not nines:\n        return grid\n\n    rows9 = {r for r, c in nines}\n    cols9 = {c for r, c in nines}\n\n    # Vertical line of 9s -> compress each row horizontally (to the left)\n    if len(cols9) == 1:\n        col9 = min(cols9)\n        res = [[0] * C for _ in range(R)]\n        for r in range(R):\n            left = [grid[r][c] for c in range(col9) if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != 9]\n            right = [grid[r][c] for c in range(col9 + 1, C) if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != 9]\n            # place left side compressed to the left\n            for i, v in enumerate(left):\n                res[r][i] = v\n            res[r][col9] = 9\n            # place right side compressed to the right\n            for i, v in enumerate(right):\n                res[r][C - len(right) + i] = v\n        return res\n\n    # Horizontal line of 9s -> compress each column vertically (upward)\n    if len(rows9) == 1:\n        row9 = min(rows9)\n        res = [[0] * C for _ in range(R)]\n        for c in range(C):\n            top = [grid[r][c] for r in range(row9) if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != 9]\n            bottom = [grid[r][c] for r in range(row9 + 1, R) if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != 9]\n            for i, v in enumerate(top):\n                res[i][c] = v\n            res[row9][c] = 9\n            for i, v in enumerate(bottom):\n                res[R - len(bottom) + i][c] = v\n        return res\n\n    # Diagonal line of 9s (r + c = const) -> compress along anti-diagonals (r - c = const)\n    # toward the top-left\n    res = [[0] * C for _ in range(R)]\n    for r, c in nines:\n        res[r][c] = 9\n\n    diag = {}\n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v != 0 and v != 9:\n                k = r - c\n                diag.setdefault(k, []).append((r, c, v))\n\n    for k, cells in diag.items():\n        # order from top-left to bottom-right along the anti-diagonal\n        cells.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n        vals = [v for _, _, v in cells]\n        # generate all coordinates on this anti-diagonal that are not 9\n        positions = []\n        if k >= 0:\n            rr, cc = k, 0\n        else:\n            rr, cc = 0, -k\n        while rr < R and cc < C:\n            if res[rr][cc] != 9:\n                positions.append((rr, cc))\n            rr += 1\n            cc += 1\n        # fill from the top-left of the anti-diagonal\n        for i, v in enumerate(vals):\n            if i < len(positions):\n                rr, cc = positions[i]\n                res[rr][cc] = v\n    return res\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return grid\n    R = len(grid)\n    C = len(grid[0])\n    nines = [(r, c) for r in range(R) for c in range(C) if grid[r][c] == 9]\n    if not nines:\n        return grid\n\n    rows9 = {r for r, c in nines}\n    cols9 = {c for r, c in nines}\n\n    # Vertical line of 9s -> compress each row horizontally (to the left)\n    if len(cols9) == 1:\n        col9 = min(cols9)\n        res = [[0] * C for _ in range(R)]\n        for r in range(R):\n            left = [grid[r][c] for c in range(col9) if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != 9]\n            right = [grid[r][c] for c in range(col9 + 1, C) if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != 9]\n            # place left side compressed to the left\n            for i, v in enumerate(left):\n                res[r][i] = v\n            res[r][col9] = 9\n            # place right side compressed to the right\n            for i, v in enumerate(right):\n                res[r][C - len(right) + i] = v\n        return res\n\n    # Horizontal line of 9s -> compress each column vertically (upward)\n    if len(rows9) == 1:\n        row9 = min(rows9)\n        res = [[0] * C for _ in range(R)]\n        for c in range(C):\n            top = [grid[r][c] for r in range(row9) if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != 9]\n            bottom = [grid[r][c] for r in range(row9 + 1, R) if grid[r][c] != 0 and grid[r][c] != 9]\n            for i, v in enumerate(top):\n                res[i][c] = v\n            res[row9][c] = 9\n            for i, v in enumerate(bottom):\n                res[R - len(bottom) + i][c] = v\n        return res\n\n    # Diagonal line of 9s (r + c = const) -> compress along anti-diagonals (r - c = const)\n    # toward the top-left\n    res = [[0] * C for _ in range(R)]\n    for r, c in nines:\n        res[r][c] = 9\n\n    diag = {}\n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v != 0 and v != 9:\n                k = r - c\n                diag.setdefault(k, []).append((r, c, v))\n\n    for k, cells in diag.items():\n        # order from top-left to bottom-right along the anti-diagonal\n        cells.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n        vals = [v for _, _, v in cells]\n        # generate all coordinates on this anti-diagonal that are not 9\n        positions = []\n        if k >= 0:\n            rr, cc = k, 0\n        else:\n            rr, cc = 0, -k\n        while rr < R and cc < C:\n            if res[rr][cc] != 9:\n                positions.append((rr, cc))\n            rr += 1\n            cc += 1\n        # fill from the top-left of the anti-diagonal\n        for i, v in enumerate(vals):\n            if i < len(positions):\n                rr, cc = positions[i]\n                res[rr][cc] = v\n    return res",
